# Inline text links

In running text, links stay on the surrounding alphabetic baseline.

Canonical classes: [`lib/text-link.ts`](../../lib/text-link.ts) (`TEXT_LINK_CLASS`, `TEXT_LINK_ICON_CLASS`).

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — inline link; icon uses vertical-align
<a href={href} className={TEXT_LINK_CLASS}>
  <Icon className={cn(TEXT_LINK_ICON_CLASS, "mr-1")} />
  tfl-ts
</a>
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — flex synthesises a box baseline from the SVG bottom and lifts the text
<a href={href} className="inline-flex items-center underline">
  <Icon className="size-4" />
  tfl-ts
</a>
```

- Do **not** use `inline-flex items-center` (or `items-baseline` with an icon-first child) on links inside sentences or headings.
- `vertical-align` / `align-[-0.15em]` does nothing on flex children — that is why the icon class is `inline-block`.
- `inline-flex items-center` is for chrome (header, buttons, chips), not prose.
- Do not put `text-box: trim-both cap alphabetic` on prose links; that trim is for chip optical centering.
